CLI.md §3.5, API.md F9 (log-2026-09-24 "canon test review calls"): a comparison is known by its
operator: an empty String operand still prints `expected:` and `got:`, with no trailing space.
-- args --
test
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

test "empty operands" {
  let e = ""
  expect e == "x"
  expect e != ""
}
-- want --
[exit 1]
[stdout]
FAIL  a/a.canon:4  empty operands
  a/a.canon:6  expect e == "x"
  expected: x
  got:
  a/a.canon:7  expect e != ""
  expected: !=
  got:

0 passed, 1 failed (…)
